> f(x: u8) = [10,20,30][x]
> domain f
domain of f:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 <= x < 3  (table index)
  defined at 3 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..2
  undefined e.g. at x=3; x=4; x=5; x=6
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range f
range of f -> int:
  10..30
  fits in u5
  undefined at 253 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
> g(x: u8 in 0..2) = [10,20,30][x]
> domain g
domain of g:
  x: u8, 0..2
  requires 0 <= x < 3  (table index)
  defined at 3 of 3 points
  over all 3 points of the domain
> range g
range of g -> int:
  10..30
  fits in u5
  over all 3 points of the domain
> h(x: u8) = 1 << x
> domain h
domain of h:
  x: u8, 0..255
  requires 0 <= x < 8  (shift amount; C UB otherwise)
  defined at 8 of 256 points
  defined for: 0..7
  undefined e.g. at x=8; x=9; x=10; x=11
  C undefined behaviour at 248 points, e.g. x=8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> range h
range of h -> u8:
  1..128   (8 distinct values)
  values: 1..2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128
  fits in u8
  undefined at 248 points
  over all 256 points of the domain
